/*---------------------------------------------------------------------------*\
  ctrl23_fedbatch_yeast_mazzoleni2015 -- an aerobic fed-batch of yeast, from a
  published model with every parameter printed.

  SOURCE (read in full, CC BY 4.0): Mazzoleni S, Landi C, Cartenì F, de Alteriis
  E, Giannino F, Paciello L, Parascandola P, "A novel process-based model of
  microbial growth: self-inhibition in Saccharomyces cerevisiae aerobic
  fed-batch cultures", Microb. Cell Fact. 14 (2015) 109,
  doi:10.1186/s12934-015-0295-4.  READ: Eq 1-7 (the seven mass balances), Table
  1 (the rate laws), Table 2 (the auxiliary equations), Table 3 (initial values
  and feed set-up) and Table 4 (all parameters, four strains), and the Methods
  paragraphs on the CEN.PK cultures.  NOT READ: the figures as data (Figs 2-7
  are plots only), the paper's supplementary files, the optimisation of the
  calibration.

  WHICH RUN.  CEN.PK113-7D, the prototroph of Fig 4: feed 500 g/l glucose, mu =
  0.16 1/h, feeding from t_F = 17 h to t_END = 49 h, the M_F and y_R of its Table 3.
  Why this one: it is the run whose biomass reaches the highest density (about
  100 g/l), so the inhibitor feedback that is the paper's point acts; it is a
  new experiment of the paper's own, with the three measured variables of its
  figure; and the concentrated feed keeps the volume change small.  The paper
  ran the strain with its own set of Table 4 values, used here without change.

  THE MODEL.  Seven pools in grams: G glucose, P glycolysis products, E ethanol,
  C_M carbon metabolites (the cell material, B = P + C_M the active mass), I
  inhibitor, R reserves, D dead cells.
      dG/dt = Feeding - Uptake
      dP/dt = eta_G Uptake - Resp_P - Ferm - Accum - Death_P
      dE/dt = eta_FE Ferm - Resp_E
      dC_M/dt = eta_RP Resp_P + eta_RE Resp_E + eta_FP Ferm - Secretion - Death_CM
      dR/dt = eta_A Accum - Death_R        dI/dt = Secretion
      dD/dt = Death_P + Death_CM + Death_R
  The laws are in constant/reactions, one reaction per process (eight), each an
  `expression` law with every Table 4 value and its table reference beside it.

  HOW THE ENGINE CARRIES IT.  (1) A `dynamicCSTR` with `volumeMode variable`
  and a zero outflow IS a fed-batch vessel: it fills and its volume follows the
  inventory, so every c[i] = n_i / V is the paper's [G] = G/V.  (2) Each pool is
  a mass-unit pseudo-component (MW = 1, volume ~ 0), so kmol are kg and kmol/m3
  are g/l; the water is real and carries the volume.  (3) The paper's efficiencies
  eta < 1 lose mass; the lost part is the named component `lostMass` (about 14
  to 20 % of each flux), so the mass balance closes and the case shows what the
  paper leaves untold.  (4) The exponential feed F0 exp(mu (t - t_F)) of Table 2
  is a `Signal` staircase on the vessel's inflow, 64 steps of half an hour whose
  value is the EXACT MEAN of the exponential over the step, so the volume fed at
  every step boundary is exact (the feed rate within a step is flat: this is the
  discretisation, 0.16 1/h x 0.5 h = 8 % between steps).  (5) The vessel is
  adiabatic and all pool records share one formation datum: no metabolic heat
  (the paper has none), so T stays at 303.15 K.

  WHAT THE PAPER'S TABLE 2 GIVES FOR V(t) is not used as printed.  It reads
  V = M_F/(c_F y_R) exp(mu (t - t_F)) , a few ml at t_F for this run, the volume of
  FEED that has entered when F0 = M_F mu/(c_F y_R) is integrated -- but the
  vessel held 1 l (Methods) at t_F, which is V_0.  The case uses the
  mass-conserving form V = V_0 + (M_F/(c_F y_R)) (exp(mu (t - t_F)) - 1), which
  is what the staircase integrates to, and reproduces the paper's reported
  ~100 g/l at 40 h.

  WHAT IS NOT MODELLED, from the paper itself: oxygen, pH, the base added for pH
  control, antifoam and the volume they add; the evaporation of ethanol; the
  sampling.  The paper's data are NOT reproduced as a pinned anchor: Fig 4 gives
  mass, glucose and ethanol as curves, and the comparison in README.md is
  information, read off the figure by eye.
\*---------------------------------------------------------------------------*/

units
(
    {
        name        reactor;
        type        dynamicCSTR;
        in          feed;
        outputs     ( broth );

        operation
        {
            volumeMode  variable;

            geometry
            {
                shape       verticalCylinder;
                diameter    0.1 m;              // area 7.854e-3 m2: 1 l = 0.127 m, 3.4 l = 0.43 m
                height      0.8 m;              // the overflow level (never reached)
            }

            outflow
            {
                mode        flow;
                F           0.0 kmol/s;         // nothing leaves: a FED-batch vessel
            }
        }

        reactions
        (
            uptake  respirationP  fermentation  respirationE  accumulation
            secretion  deathP  deathCM  deathR
        );
    }
);

controllers
